{
  "_id": "fVhTiaW18HafUZGQ",
  "name": "Know-It-All",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-open-purple.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<blockquote><p><em>There is no subject on which you lack an opinion, and irritatingly, you are usually right. Locks, languages, lineages, poisons, the tensile strength of a rope bridge: you have read about all of it, and you will explain it now whether or not anyone asked.</em></p></blockquote>\n<p><strong>1st Level</strong></p><ul><li>You do not gain Skill Increases. Instead you are Trained in all non-Lore skills.</li><li>You are Trained in Universal Lore, a Lore skill that can be used only to Recall Knowledge, but on any topic. It counts as an applicable Lore for Recall Knowledge DCs.</li><li>You gain two extra Skill Feats every level.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>2nd Level</strong></p><ul><li>Expert in all non-Lore skills and Universal Lore.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>5th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Once per turn, you may Recall Knowledge as a free action.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>7th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Master in all non-Lore skills and Universal Lore.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>15th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Legendary in all non-Lore skills and Universal Lore.</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>In Foundry:</strong> every non-Lore skill is at least Trained, Expert from 2nd, Master from 7th and Legendary from 15th. Universal Lore appears among your Lore skills, Intelligence-based, on the same ranks. A <em>Know-It-All</em> feat group with two skill feat slots per level appears on your Feats tab.</p>\n<p>For the table: do not spend your class's skill increases. Use Universal Lore only to Recall Knowledge; against a creature, the GM picks one of the two Applicable Lore DCs on its sheet. Recall Knowledge as a free action once per turn from 5th.</p>",
      "gm": ""
    },
